    "created_at": "2026-11-07T00:37:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T00:37:17Z",
    "body": "Patch held (staged in an agent worktree, not yet committed). The cause: sim::verify::section::tangency read a Boundary-mode straight move only at its end point (laws::law_points). The solid law (b2) did not catch it either, even with the mesh present: the pinned chord read clean with model Some and with model None. The fix adds section::wall_gouge. In Mode::Boundary every straight cutting move (arcs excluded) is also measured along its whole length (laws::dist2_segs), but only against WALL edges: (1) every edge of the model section is a wall; (2) with a model, a region edge is a wall when the section contains a point 0.05 mm off its midpoint on either side, so a Face rim over air is open; (3) with no model there is no material to probe, so a move that properly crosses a region edge is treated as an open-rim overrun (a Face row) and keeps the end-point reading, while a move that crosses no edge answers to every region edge. Pinned by boundary_walls::a_contour_g1_chorded_across_a_convex_wall_corner_is_a_gouge_at_that_move and boundary_walls::the_same_contour_rounding_the_corner_on_a_true_arc_is_clean, each with and without the mesh. These suites are still green: area_controls (both Face tests), area_open, verify, operations, golden_cl, real_tip_contour, and quick tier. Known limit, logged in RECOMMENDED.md: without a mesh, a straight move that crosses a 2.5-D contour's wall (its centre inside the material) is still excused, as it was before this change.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
